   "he": "וְלֹא בְּכָלָךְ. אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: שְׁאֵלְתִּינְהוּ לְכׇל נָחוֹתֵי יַמָּא וְאָמְרִי (לַהּ) כּוּלְכָא שְׁמֵיהּ. רַב יִצְחָק בַּר זְעֵירָא אָמַר: גּוּשְׁקְרָא.",
   "en": "«And» we also learned in the mishna that «one may not» light «with kalakh. Shmuel said: I asked all seafarers, and they said to me» that the present-day «name» of kalakh mentioned in the mishna «is kulka. Rav Yitzḥak bar Ze’ira said:» Kalakh is «the cocoon of the silkworm [gushkera].»"
  }
